{"availability":"available","full":"jymchng/sosecrets-rs","name":"sosecrets-rs","description":"A simple `Secret` wrapper type that reveals the secret at most `N: typenum::Unsigned` (i.e. unsigned integer) times with compile time guarantees and exposure of secrets are strictly controlled in its lifetime.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":18,"forks":0,"created":"2023-11-16T16:18:11Z","updated":"2024-07-18T17:36:11Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2021&gist=3c2e97e284c60c8a4067b77b6cfd72c7","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:20:12.534Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T13:20:12.534Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T13:20:12.534Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T13:20:12.534Z","stars":18,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["It is similar to the secrecy crate but with type level and compile-time guarantees that the Secret value is not ’exposed’ more than MEC number of times and is only exposed under a well-defined lexical scope.","It makes use of the typenum crate for all its compile-time guarantees."],"features":["type level and compile-time guarantees and","each reference corresponds to each secret that can only be exposed or revealed under a lexical scope with an invariant lifetime","Exposure Control: Secret values can only be exposed a limited number of times, preventing unintentional information leaks. This is guaranteed at compile time. Secrets are exposed and available for use with an invariant…","Zeroization: If configured with the \"zeroize\" feature, secrets are zeroized upon dropping them.","Cloneable Secrets: With the \"cloneable-secret\" feature, Secret values can be cloned if the underlying type, T, implements the CloneableSecret trait."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jymchng/sosecrets-rs/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"1c084b604a1a210181ef2ad44cb1b960cf1008